   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# Video sharpener (NVIDIA Open-H3)\n\n**How to use**\n1. Click *choose file* in the green box **1** and pick your video.\n2. Set the output size in the green boxes **2**:\n   - 2560 x 1440 = 2K (default)\n   - 1920 x 1088 = Full HD (use 1088, not 1080)\n   - Width and height MUST be multiples of 32, otherwise a coloured line appears at the bottom.\n   - Frames: 124 = 5 s, 260 = about 10 s (always 17 x n + 5).\n3. Optional: in box **3**, write one line describing the video. It helps the AI.\n4. Press **Run**. The result appears in box **4** and is saved in the ComfyUI *output/video* folder.\n\n**Good to know**\n- The whole clip is redrawn in ONE pass, so detail stays consistent from start to end.\n- Works best on videos made by MiniMax H3. Other videos work too.\n- It *invents* believable detail. Do not use it for evidence or news footage.\n- Sound is not copied to the new video.\n"
   ],
   "title": "READ ME",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
